<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kotorosl</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kotorosl is a river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslavl">Yaroslavl</a> Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, about 130 kilometres long, flowing from Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rostov">Rostov</a> to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> at Yaroslavl. The city of Yaroslavl was founded on the headland at its mouth in the early 11th century, and the river linked the old Rostov lands with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga-trade-route">Volga trade route</a>.</p></div>
